NAME
       partx - tell the kernel about the partitions of a disk

SYNOPSIS
       partx [-a | -d | -u | -s] DISK

DESCRIPTION
       partx reads the partition table of a disk and adds, removes or
       updates partitions in the kernel's view, or just lists them. It is an
       alternative to partprobe.

OPTIONS
       -a, --add
              Tell the kernel about partitions it does not know yet.

       -d, --delete
              Tell the kernel to forget partitions.

       -u, --update
              Bring the kernel's view in line with the table on disk.

       -s, --show
              List the partitions on the disk.

EXAMPLES
           partx -u /dev/vdb

SEE ALSO
       partprobe(8), lsblk(8), fdisk(8)
